## Glossary

- [Product Owner Job Description & Role](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/product-owner-job-description-and-role): Understand the Product Owner’s responsibilities and role dynamics to enhance professional development and hiring decisions.
- [Project Manager Job Description & Role](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/project-manager-job-description-and-role): Unlock insights into the project manager role and its critical functions, essential for hiring or educational purposes globally. Stay informed with Pebl.
- [The Importance of an HR Compliance Officer in International Businesses](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hr-compliance-officer-in-international-businesses): Learn why HR Compliance Officers are essential for navigating complex global regulations and maintaining legal integrity in business.
- [What Are Advisory Shares?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/advisory-share): Advisory shares are equity offered to advisors in exchange for expertise. Learn how to use them to get support without upfront costs with Pebl.
- [What Are Back Taxes?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/back-taxes): Learn the definition and background of back taxes. Find out the consequences of owing them and how to address them to avoid penalties and interest charges.
- [What Are COBRA Benefits?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/cobra-benefits): COBRA benefits allow employees to keep their health insurance after leaving a job in the U.S. Discover how this impacts compliance with Pebl.
- [What Are Conditions of Employment?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/conditions-of-employment): Conditions of employment are the terms, requirements, and policies an employee and employer agree to as outlined in an employment agreement.
- [What Are Emerging Markets?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/emerging-markets): Emerging markets are country economies transitioning from developing status towards integration into the global economy. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Are Employee Benefits?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employee-benefits): Employee benefits are non-wage forms of compensation offered in addition to standard salaries. Get the definition and examples with Pebl.
- [What Are Employee Surveys?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employee-surveys): Learn what employee surveys are, how they capture feedback on engagement, satisfaction, and culture, and explore common survey types with Pebl.
- [What Are Flexible Workspaces?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/flexible-workspaces): Flexible workspaces allow employees to work in many ways, like with hot desks, meeting rooms, and open offices. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Are High-Income Skills?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/high-income-skills): High-income skills are specialized, in-demand abilities that command higher pay. Explore examples and what to look for when hiring with Pebl.
- [What Are In-Kind Benefits?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/in-kind-benefits): In-kind benefits are non-cash perks offered on top of salaries or wages. Learn the most popular types, plus tax implications with Pebl.
- [What Are Payroll Deductions?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/payroll-deductions): Learn what payroll deductions are with Pebl. Find out how they work, and why they’re essential to understand for compensation compliance.
- [What Are Remote Work Allowances?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/remote-work-allowance): Employers give their workforce remote work allowances as an added benefit while they work from home. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Are Social Security Wages?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/social-security-wages): Learn what Social Security wages are with Pebl. Find out what’s included or excluded, and how employers calculate and report them for taxes.
- [What Are Statutory Benefits?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/statutory-benefits): Statutory benefits are mandatory employee benefits required by law. Learn about the different types of mandatory benefits with Pebl.
- [What Are Total Rewards?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/total-rewards): Total rewards refer to a wide range of compensation, benefits, and incentives that employers offer employees for their work.
- [What Are Virtual Teams?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/virtual-teams): Virtual teams are employees who work together remotely with digital tools. Virtual teams are often distributed. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Are Voluntary Deductions?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/voluntary-deductions): Voluntary deductions are pay withholdings employees choose, like retirement contributions or insurance premiums. Explore examples and compliance tips with Pebl.
- [What Are Wages?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/wages): Wages are the monetary compensation an employee receives for their work. Learn how wages differ from salary and how to correctly calculate wages.
- [What Is 14th-Month Pay?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/14th-month-pay): 14th-month pay is a bonus payment employers give to their employees. See how it is used to reward employees, attract talent, and more.
- [What Is a 2-2-3 Schedule?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/2-2-3-schedule): Learn what a 2-2-3 schedule is with Pebl. Find out how it works and why industries like manufacturing or healthcare use it for 24/7 operations.
- [What Is a 360-Degree Feedback Survey?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/360-degree-feedback-survey): Learn what a 360-degree feedback survey is, how it gathers input from managers, peers, and direct reports, and why it provides a full view of employee effectiveness.
- [What Is a 9/80 Work Schedule?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/9-80-work-schedule): A 9/80 work schedule means working 80 hours over 9 days, earning every other Friday off. Learn how it can boost productivity with Pebl.
- [What Is a B-1 Business Visa?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/b1-visa): B-1 visas are business visas that allow travel to the U.S. temporarily. Valid for up to 10 years, holders can stay for 180 days. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Chief Human Resources Officer (CHRO)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/chief-hr-officer): CHROs oversee organizations’ HR departments and ensure HR strategies align with business goals. Learn more about CHROs with Pebl.
- [What Is a Common-Law Employee?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/common-law-employee): Discover the definition of a common-law employee and how it differs from other worker classifications in the workplace. Read on to learn the importance.
- [What Is a Compensation Analyst?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/compensation-analyst): Discover what a Compensation Analyst does and how they support fair pay and job equity. Ideal for professionals hiring globally or seeking career insights.
- [What Is a Compensation and Benefits Manager?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/compensation-and-benefits-manager): A compensation and benefits manager designs and oversees compensation structures, like salaries and benefits. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Compensation Package?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/compensation-package): A compensation package refers to the salary, benefits, and other forms of remuneration an employer offers employees for their work.
- [What Is a Compensation Policy?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/compensation-policy): A compensation policy refers to a company’s practices for providing employees with pay, benefits, and other rewards.
- [What Is a Compliance Report?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/compliance-report): Learn what a compliance report is with Pebl. Discover why it matters, and how it helps your business meet legal and regulatory requirements.
- [What Is a Compressed Work Week?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/compressed-work-week): A compressed work week allows employees to work full-time hours in fewer days. Learn about how it works and its benefits with Pebl.
- [What Is a Conditional Offer of Employment?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/conditional-offer-of-employment): A conditional offer of employment is a job offer where an employer agrees to hire a candidate if certain conditions are met. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Contingent Worker?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/contingent-worker): A contingent worker is talent that performs tasks for an organization without being formally hired as the organization’s employee.
- [What Is a Contract Employee?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/contract-employee): A contract employee, also known as a freelancer, is a self-employed individual hired to perform specific projects or services. Learn more from Pebl.
- [What Is a Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) Manager?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/corporate-social-responsibility-manager): Uncover the essential role of a Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) Manager, focusing on ethics and sustainability. Perfect for professionals hiring globally.
- [What Is a Cost-of-Living Adjustment?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/cost-of-living-adjustment-cola): A cost-of-living adjustment (COLA) increases pay to offset inflation or regional costs. Learn more about COLAs and why employers use them with Pebl.
- [What Is a Crypto Wallet?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/crypto-wallet): Learn what a crypto wallet is with Pebl. Find out how it differs from a digital wallet, and why employers should understand its role in global payroll.
- [What Is a Customer Success Manager?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/customer-success-manager): Learn what a Customer Success Manager does with Pebl. Discover how they support employers working with EORs and global HR platforms.
- [What Is a Cut-Off Date?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/cut-off-date): In accounting, a cut-off date represents the end of a financial or reporting period. Learn how to determine cut-off dates and avoid errors.
- [What Is a Decentralized Workforce?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/decentralized-workforce): A decentralized workforce is when employees work across multiple locations, often through remote work. Learn about its benefits with Pebl.
- [What Is a Defined Benefit Plan?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/defined-benefit-plan): A defined benefit plan guarantees employees a fixed income in retirement. Learn how it works and how it differs from other plans with Pebl.
- [What Is a Digital Nomad Visa?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/digital-nomad-visa): A digital nomad visa allows remote workers to live and work in a foreign country for a company outside that country. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Digital Wallet?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/digital-wallet): Learn what a digital wallet is, how employers use them for global payroll, and how employees can receive digital wallet direct deposit with Pebl.
- [What Is a Direct Report?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/direct-report): A direct report is an employee who reports directly to someone above them within a company. Anyone who works directly under someone is a direct report.
- [What Is a Disregarded Entity?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/disregarded-entity-single-member-llc): A disregarded entity is a business with a single owner that has not elected to be taxed separately. Learn about single-member LLCs with Pebl.
- [What Is a Distributed Workforce?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/distributed-workforce): A distributed workforce refers to a company’s employees who work remotely from various locations around the globe. Learn the benefits of distributed work.
- [What is a Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion (DEI) Manager?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/diversity-equity-and-inclusion-dei-manager): Discover what a Diversity Equity and Inclusion (DEI) Manager does and how they shape an organization’s culture by implementing strategic initiatives for a more inclusive workplace.
- [What Is a Divestiture?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/divestiture): A divestiture is the disposal of a company or assets through sale, exchange, closure, or bankruptcy. Learn about corporate divestitures with Pebl.
- [What Is a Document Management System?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/document-management-system): Learn what a document management system (DMS) is and how HR teams use it to track records, productivity, and compliance with Pebl.
- [What Is a DPA?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/dpa): A data processing agreement (DPA) is an agreement that regulates personal data processing conducted for business purposes.
- [What Is a Floating Holiday?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/floating-holiday): A floating holiday is paid leave that employees can use for anything and at any time outside of their allotted paid time off (PTO).
- [What Is a Foreign Legal Entity?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/foreign-legal-entity): Expansion is necessary for businesses to increase revenue, but creating a foreign legal entity can be a black hole. Learn how to do it with Pebl.
- [What Is a Foreign Subsidiary?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/foreign-subsidiaries): Foreign subsidiaries are companies that operate in one country but are owned by a company in another country. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Foreign Worker Levy?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/foreign-worker-levy): A foreign worker levy is a government-mandated fee employers must pay when they hire a foreign employee in certain markets.
- [What Is a Foreign-Invested Enterprise (FIE)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/foreign-invested-enterprise-fie): Foreign Invested Enterprises (FIE) are businesses that are partially or wholly funded by foreign investors. Learn about FIE types and more with Pebl.
- [What Is a General Ledger?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/general-ledger): Learn what a general ledger is, how it records financial transactions by account, and why it’s essential for keeping your books accurate.
- [What Is a Global Contractor?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/global-contractor): A global contractor offers services to a company while residing in a different country than the business. Learn tips and risks of hiring global contractors.
- [What Is a Global Employment Organization (GEO)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/geo): A global employment organization (GEO) is a third-party company that provides international employment solutions for companies to hire, pay, and manage global talent.
- [What Is a Global HR Manager?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/global-hr-manager): A global HR manager manages HR functions across multiple countries, navigating diverse cultural norms, and labor laws. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Global HR Policy Analyst?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/global-hr-policy-analyst): Uncover the vital role of a Global HR Policy Analyst in shaping workforce strategies. Discover key responsibilities and skills for global workforce management.
- [What Is a Global Mobility Manager?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/global-mobility-manager): Global mobility managers oversee relocation, immigration, tax compliance, compensation, housing, and more. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Global Onboarding Specialist?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/global-onboarding-specialist): What is a Global Onboarding Specialist? Uncover detailed insights into this key role in global hiring, including opportunities, required skills, and ways they enhance hiring...
- [What Is a Global Payroll Manager?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/global-payroll-manager): A global payroll manager manages payroll across multiple countries, ensuring compliance with tax laws and regulations. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Global Team?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/what-global-team): Global teams are employees who work remotely around the world. Managing a global team comes with unique pros and cons. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Global Workforce?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/global-workforce): A global workforce is a group of employees working for the same company but across the world. Explore global worker benefits and more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Green Card?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/green-card): Green cards are a name for the ID card issued to permanent residents in the U.S. who can stay indefinitely. Learn about green cards with Pebl.
- [What Is a Health Savings Account?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/health-savings-account): An HSA is a tax-advantaged account employers offer to employees to save for medical expenses. Learn how HSAs support retention with Pebl.
- [What Is a Human Capital Consultant in Growing Organizations?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/human-capital-consultant-in-growing-organizations): Uncover the benefits of Human Capital Consultants for growing businesses. See how these experts maximize human potential and support global hiring.
- [What is a Job Description?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/job-description): A job description defines role duties, responsibilities, and qualifications. Learn its purpose in hiring, compliance, and performance management with Pebl.
- [What Is a Labor Relations Manager?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/labor-relations-manager): A labor relations manager oversees the relationship between employers and employees, particularly in unionized settings. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What is a Learning and Development Manager?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/learning-and-development-manager): Discover the role of a Learning and Development Manager—explore their responsibilities, career path, and the skills needed to succeed.
- [What Is a Learning Experience Designer?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/learning-experience-designer): Discover what a Learning Experience Designer does and explore the distinct skills needed in this innovative career path compared to Instructional Designers.
- [What Is a Learning Management System (LMS)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/learning-management-system): A learning management system (LMS) helps train, onboard, and develop teams. Learn how it supports global workforce growth with Pebl.
- [What Is a Leave of Absence?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/leave-of-absence): Get the meaning of leave of absence and the types available depending on your situation. Explore leave of absence policies and more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Long-Term Incentive Plan (LTIP)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/long-term-incentive-plan-ltip): A long-term incentive plan (LTIP) rewards employees based on multiyear performance. Learn how they work and their benefits with Pebl.
- [What Is a Market Adjustment Raise?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/market-adjustment-raise): A market adjustment raise aligns employee pay with current market rates. Learn when they are offered, their impacts, and more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Merit Increase?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/merit-increase): Learn what a merit increase is with Pebl. Find out how it works, and how employers can use it to reward employees and drive retention.
- [What Is a Non-Compete Agreement?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/non-compete-agreement): A non-compete agreement prevents employees from working with competitors after leaving a company. Learn how they work and why they are used from Pebl.
- [What Is a Non-Employee?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/non-employee): A non-employee is an individual who works for an organization but is not formally employed by that organization. Learn how to ensure proper worker classification.
- [What Is a Non-Exempt Employee?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/non-exempt-employees): Learn about non-exempt employees with Pebl. Find out what employers must know about overtime, pay, and compliance.
- [What Is a Notice Period?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/notice-period): A notice period is the time between the notification of an employee’s resignation or termination and the employee’s last day of employment.
- [What Is a Pay Period?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/pay-period): A pay period is the timeframe during which employees work and earn wages. Learn pay period types and how to determine a pay period.
- [What Is a Payout?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/payout): A payout is the transfer of funds, assets, or benefits to individuals, entities, or investors. Explore the meaning of payout and more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Payroll Cycle?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/payroll-cycle): A payroll cycle is the frequency at which an employer pays employees. Bi-weekly payroll is common in the U.S. and monthly payroll is common globally.
- [What Is a Payroll Register?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/payroll-register): Learn what a payroll register is with Pebl. Explore how employers use it to maintain accurate payroll, track expenses, and ensure compliance.
- [What Is a Payroll Report?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/payroll-report): Learn what a payroll report is from Pebl. Find out how they help employers track pay, deductions, and tax responsibilities to stay compliant.
- [What Is a Payslip?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/payslip): A payslip is a statement outlining the details of an employee’s pay during a set pay period.
- [What Is a People Analytics Manager?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/people-analytics-manager): Explore the essential duties of a People Analytics Manager and how they leverage data analytics to optimize human resource management and strategy.
- [What Is a People Operations Specialist?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/people-operations-specialist): Discover what a People Operations Specialist does, including key responsibilities and how they leverage EOR software for global hiring strategies.
- [What Is a Performance Bonus?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/performance-bonus): A performance bonus is an incentive provided by employers to employees based on individual, team, or company-wide achievements and contributions.
- [What Is a Performance Management Cycle?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/performance-management-cycle): A performance management cycle sets goals, tracks progress, and reviews employee performance. Learn how it supports growth with Pebl.
- [What is a Performance Management System?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/performance-management-system): Learn what a performance management system is with Pebl. Discover how it helps employers with employee goals, productivity, and growth.
- [What Is a Personality Hire?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/personality-hire): A personality hire is chosen for their energy, attitude, or cultural impact, not just qualifications. Learn how they shape team dynamics with Pebl.
- [What Is a Probationary Period?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/probationary-period): A probationary period occurs at the beginning of a new hire’s employment, during which the employer evaluates their performance. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Recruitment Marketing Specialist?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/recruitment-marketing-specialist): Discover how a Recruitment Marketing Specialist leads to an organizations success. Learn the essential roles, responsibilities, and how to create effective job descriptions today.
- [What is a Recruitment Operations Manager?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/recruitment-operations-manager): A recruitment operations manager oversees an entire recruitment process, develops strategies to find new employees and more. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Relocation Package?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/relocation-package): A relocation package assists employees in moving. Learn what a reasonable and typical relocation package includes and get examples with Pebl.
- [What Is a Remote Work Coordinator?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/remote-work-coordinator): Uncover the responsibilities of a Remote Work Coordinator to enhance your remote team's efficiency and communication strategies today.
- [What Is a Remote-First Company?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/remote-first-company): Learn what a remote-first company is and how it differs from a hybrid model. See why more employers are choosing it and how Pebl can help.
- [What Is a Residence Permit?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/residence-permit): A residence permit allows one to live in a country for a specified period of time. Permit details vary by country. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Rotational Assignment?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/rotational-assignment): A rotational assignment is when an employee is given a different job within an organization and can involve relocating. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Sabbatical?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/sabbatical): A sabbatical is a paid or unpaid break from work to recharge or pursue goals. Understand how it works, when it’s offered, and why it’s gaining popularity.
- [What Is a Salaried Employee?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/salaried-employee): A salaried employee receives a fixed amount of pay, regardless of hours worked. Learn about salaried positions and salary workers with Pebl.
- [What Is a Salary Review?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/salary-review): A salary review is the process of evaluating an employee’s salary to ensure it is competitive, fair, and accurately reflects their work performance.
- [What Is a Secondment?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/secondment): A secondment is when an employer temporarily assigns an employee to a new position. Learn how secondments benefit employees and teams.
- [What Is a Skills Gap Analysis?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/skills-gap-analysis): A skills gap analysis identifies employee skills and new skills needed to meet an organization's goals. Explore skills gap assessments with Pebl.
- [What Is a Stipend?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/stipend): Discover what a stipend is and how it works. Pebl explains the benefits, tax rules, and key differences between stipends and wages.
- [What Is a Stock Grant?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/stock-grant): Stock grants are a form of compensation for employees, in which an employer gives employees corporate stock in the company as part of an equity plan.
- [What Is a Succession Plan?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/succession-plan): A succession plan prepares companies for leadership transitions. Learn what it is, why it matters, and how to maintain stability during transitions with Pebl.
- [What is a SWIFT Payment?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/swift-payment): SWIFT payments are a secure, electronic way to send and receive money internationally. Learn about their benefits with Pebl.
- [What Is a System of Record?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/sor-system-of-record): A System of Record (SOR) stores official business data like HR or financial records. Discover its role in compliance, reporting, and tech stacks with Pebl.
- [What Is a Talent Acquisition Manager?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/talent-acquisition-manager): A talent acquisition manager oversees sourcing, identifying, attracting, and hiring the best candidates to fill open positions. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Tax Identification Number (TIN)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/tax-identification-number): Learn about Tax Identification Numbers (TINs). Get the definition, uses, and how they help identify taxpayers, including SSNs, ITINs, and EINs with Pebl.
- [What Is a Temporary Employee?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/temporary-employee): A temporary employee is someone who is hired to work for a predetermined amount of time. Learn the benefits of hiring temp employees with Pebl.
- [What Is a Total Rewards Manager?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/total-rewards-manager): Total rewards managers design and implement employee reward strategies, which include salaries, benefits, and more. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Tripartite Agreement?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/tripartite-agreement): Tripartite agreements, or tri-party agreements, refer to any legal agreement between three separate parties. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Virtual Employee?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/virtual-employee): A virtual employee is someone who conducts their work online and remotely from the company’s location. Learn the benefits and challenges of virtual staffing.
- [What Is a Visa Stamp?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/visa-stamp): Learn what a visa stamp is with Pebl. Find out how it differs from a visa, and why it matters for global employers and remote employees alike.
- [What Is a Visa Support Letter?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/visa-support-letter): A visa support letter is a formal document from an employer confirming a worker’s job and purpose of travel. Learn how to write one with Pebl's template.
- [What Is a W-2 Employee?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/w-2-employee): A W-2 employee is a formally employed individual working for a company or organization in the U.S. Read more for answers to your W-2 FAQs.
- [What Is a Wholly-Owned Subsidiary?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/wholly-owned-subsidiary): A wholly-owned subsidiary is a company that is entirely owned and controlled by another company, known as the parent company.
- [What Is a Work Permit?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/work-permit): A work permit is a government-issued document that authorizes an individual to work in a specific country. Learn about how work permits work with Pebl.
- [What Is a Work Visa?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/work-visa): A work visa is a legal document allowing a foreign national to work in a specific country for a designated time. Explore permit requirements with Pebl.
- [What Is a Work-From-Anywhere (WFA) Job?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/work-from-anywhere-job): Work-from-anywhere jobs are shaping the future of employment by trading offices for more flexibility and productivity. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Workforce Planning Manager?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/workforce-planning-manager): A workforce planning manager analyzes and forecasts workforce needs, aligning employees with an organization’s set strategy. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is a Working Holiday Visa?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/working-holiday-visa): Learn what a working holiday visa is with Pebl. Discover who qualifies, and how employers can compliantly hire short-term international talent.
- [What Is a Zero-Hour Contract?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/zero-hour-contract): A zero-hour contract is an employment contract that stipulates an employer does not have to provide an employee with a minimum or guaranteed number of working hours.
- [What Is Absenteeism?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/absenteeism): Absenteeism is frequent unplanned absence from work. Learn its causes, employer costs, and why accurate tracking is critical for payroll with Pebl.
- [What Is Accrued Payroll?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/accrued-payroll): Accrued payroll refers to all forms of payroll compensation that a business owes its employees but has not yet paid out.
- [What Is Adaptability in the Workplace?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/adaptability-in-the-workplace): Adaptability in the workplace is the quality of being able to adapt to new conditions. Learn tips on how to navigate change at work with Pebl.
- [What Is an A1 Certificate?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/a1-certificate): An A1 certificate verifies where an employee pays their social security. Learn about when and where they are required and how to apply for one with Pebl.
- [What Is an Accredited Employer Work Visa?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/accredited-employer-work-visa): An accredited employer work visa lets approved businesses hire overseas workers. Learn how to apply, and how to sponsor employees with Pebl.
- [What Is an Acquihire?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/acquihire): An acquihire is a business acquisition to gain another company's employees, rather than their products, services, and technology. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is an Affiliate Company?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/affiliate-company): An affiliate company is a minority shareholder in another company. In most cases, affiliate companies possess less than 50% ownership. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is an Agent of Record (AOR)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/agent-of-record): An agent of record, also known as a broker of record or AOR, is an entity with legal authority to represent an insured party and manage an insurance policy on its behalf.
- [What Is an Agile Workforce?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/agile-workforce): An agile workforce can adapt to changes, acquire new skills, and work flexibly in response to business needs. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is an Annuity?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/annuity): Understand the definition of an annuity with Pebl. Learn about types of annuities such as fixed, variable, and indexed, and how annuities work.
- [What Is an Applicant Tracking System?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/applicant-tracking-system): Learn what an applicant tracking system (ATS) is and how Pebl integrates with top platforms to streamline global hiring and onboarding.
- [What is an Employee Assistance Program (EAP)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employee-assistance-program): Employee assistance programs provide counseling to employees with issues that impact their performance. Learn about EAPs with Pebl.
- [What Is an Employee Engagement Survey?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employee-engagement-survey): Learn what an employee engagement survey is, how it measures motivation and commitment, and why it matters for improving employee experience with Pebl.
- [What is an Employee Experience Manager?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employee-experience-manager): Uncover the role of an Employee Experience Manager in shaping engaging workplaces that cultivate higher employee morale and efficiency.
- [What Is an Employee Portal?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employee-portal): Learn what an employee portal is with Pebl. Find out how it supports self-service HR, and how employers can set one up for global teams.
- [What Is an Employee Transfer?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employee-transfer): An employee transfer is the process of moving an employee from one position, department, or location to another. Learn employee transfer tips in our guide.
- [What Is an Employee Value Proposition?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employee-value-proposition): Employee value propositions are outlines of the benefits and rewards that companies offer their employees. Learn about EVP with Pebl.
- [What Is an Employee Wellness Program?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employee-wellness-program): Learn about what employee wellness programs are, what their benefits are, and why they are important for remote employees with Pebl.
- [What is an Employer Branding Specialist?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employer-branding-specialist): An employer branding specialist develops and implements strategies to create a positive image of an employer. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is an Employer Identification Number (EIN)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employer-identification-number): An Employer identification number (EIN) is also known as a federal tax identification number and is used to identify a business entity. Learn more from Pebl.
- [What is an Employer of Record B](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/what-employer-record-b): Interdum at semper amet consectetur vulputate duis viverra pretium mauris.
- [What Is an Employment Agreement?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employment-agreement): An employment agreement is a contract between an employer and an employee that defines the terms and conditions of employment.
- [What Is an Employment Authorization Document?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employment-authorization-document): An EAD is a U.S.-only work permit for eligible noncitizens. Discover who can apply, and how it differs from visas and green cards with Pebl.
- [What Is an Equity Incentive Plan?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/equity-incentive-plan): An equity incentive plan offers employees shares of the company as supplemental compensation, which is awarded through stocks, warrants, or bonds.
- [What Is an EU Blue Card?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/eu-blue-card): Discover how the EU Blue Card helps employers attract non-EU talent with Pebl. Learn about EU Blue Card benefits, requirements, and how to apply.
- [What Is an Exempt Employee?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/exempt-employee): Learn what an exempt employee is with Pebl. Find out how it differs from being salaried, and why accurate classification matters for overtime.
- [What Is an Exit Interview?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/exit-interview): Exit interviews are conversations used to gather feedback from employees who are leaving. Learn how to run them and turn feedback into better decisions.
- [What Is an Expatriate Employee?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/expatriate-employee): Expatriate employees are people who are living or working in countries where they are not citizens. Learn what hiring expats entails with Pebl.
- [What Is an H-1B Visa?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/h1b-visa): Navigating the visa process for international employees is difficult. Find answers with Pebl’s guide to the H-1B visa application process.
- [What Is an Hourly Employee?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hourly-employee): An hourly employee is paid for the hours they work, not a fixed salary. Learn how hourly pay, overtime, and compliance work across teams.
- [What Is an HPI Visa?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hpi-visa): The HPI visa is a UK work visa for high‑potential graduates from top global universities. Learn eligibility rules, benefits, and how to apply for an HPI visa from Pebl.
- [What Is an HR Budget?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hr-budget): An HR budget outlines the costs of hiring, compensation, benefits, and compliance. Learn how it works and how to build one that works with Pebl.
- [What Is an HR Business Analyst?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hr-business-analyst): An HR business analyst collects and analyzes HR data to identify trends, provide insights, and make recommendations. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is an HR Business Partner (HRBP)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hr-business-partner): Human Resources Business Partners align HR strategies with business goals. Learn about what an HRBP’s responsibilities include, with Pebl.
- [What Is an HR Compliance Manager?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hr-compliance-manager): An HR compliance manager ensures that HR practices comply with employment laws, regulations, and internal policies. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is an HR Coordinator? A Guide to the Role and Career Path](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hr-coordinator): Explore the role of an HR Coordinator in 2025. Discover key responsibilities, career paths, and how EOR software can aid global hiring.
- [What Is an HR Director?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hr-director): An HR Director oversees HR tasks like legal compliance, workforce management and providing advice to leadership. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is an HR Generalist?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hr-generalist): HR generalists manage recruitment, employee relations, benefits administration, onboarding, and more. Learn about HR generalists with Pebl.
- [What is an HR Policy Manager?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hr-policy-manager): Discover what an HR Policy Manager does, and the essential skills needed to manage effective HR policies and strategies in a global environment with Pebl.
- [What Is an HR Specialist?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hr-specialist): HR specialists focus on specific areas of HR, like recruitment, training, or compensation and benefits. Learn about HR specialists with Pebl.
- [What Is an HR Technology Manager?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hr-technology-manager): Learn what an HR Technology Manager does, key responsibilities and skills, and how they lead HR digital transformation to support seamless global hiring.
- [What Is an HRIS Manager?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hris-manager): An HRIS manager oversees and maintains a company’s Human Resources Information System (HRIS). Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is an Identity Provider (IdP)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/identity-provider-idp): An identity provider verifies users and shares trusted login data with apps. Learn how it helps your team manage access more securely.
- [What Is an Immigration Consultant?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/immigration-consultant): An immigration consultant provides non-legal advice to people who want to emigrate to another country. Learn about immigration agents with Pebl.
- [What Is an Indefinite Employment Contract?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/indefinite-contracts): An indefinite contract is a type of employment contract that has no end date. Learn the pros, cons, alternatives, and requirements with Pebl.
- [What is an L1 Visa?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/l1-visa): L1 visas are nonimmigrant visas that allow foreign companies to temporarily transfer employees to work in the U.S. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is an LLC?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/llc-limited-liability-company): An LLC is a business structure that protects owners from personal liability while offering tax and management flexibility. Learn how LLCs work with Pebl.
- [What Is an NDA?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/nda-non-disclosure-agreement): Learn what an NDA is with Pebl. Find out how employers use non-disclosure agreements to protect information, IP, and confidential data.
- [What Is an O-1 Visa?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/o-1-visa): The O-1 visa allows top talent to work in the U.S. Explore eligibility, application criteria, how it differs from other visas, benefits, and more with Pebl.
- [What Is an Org Chart?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/organizational-chart): An org chart is a visual tool that outlines a company’s structure, showing roles, reporting lines, and hierarchy. Learn how org charts support clarity.
- [What is an Organizational Development Manager?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/organizational-development-manager): Discover what an Organizational Development Manager does. Learn about roles, responsibilities, and skills needed for effective change management in HR.
- [What Is an SEP IRA?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/sep-ira): Learn about SEP-IRAs, high contribution limit retirement plans for small business owners and the self-employed, and how they work with Pebl.
- [What Is Annualized Salary?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/annualized-salary): An annualized salary is an estimate of how much an employee will earn over a year based on their wages and time spent on the job.
- [What is Asynchronous Communication?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/asynchronous-communication): Asynchronous communication is any means of communication that isn’t immediately back-and-forth, like email or texting. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is At-Will Employment?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/at-will-employment): In the U.S., at-will employment means employers or employees can terminate work anytime. Explore pros, cons, and key protections with Pebl.
- [What Is Attrition in HR?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/attrition-in-hr): Learn what attrition means in HR with Pebl. Explore how to measure it, its impact on your workforce, and how employers can monitor and reduce it.
- [What Is Automated Expense Reporting?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/automated-expense-reporting): Automated expense reporting software simplifies tracking and reimbursements. Discover how it streamlines HR and finance tasks with Pebl.
- [What Is Back Pay?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/back-pay): Back pay is any form of unpaid compensation an employer owes an employee. Learn about back pay taxes, how to calculate it, and more from Pebl.
- [What Is Base Pay?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/base-pay): Base pay is the fixed salary or hourly wage employees earn before bonuses or benefits. Learn how it relates to net pay, gross pay, and total compensation with Pebl.
- [What Is Bi-Weekly Payroll?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/bi-weekly-payroll): Bi-weekly payroll is when employees receive paychecks on a specific day every two weeks. Learn how to calculate biweekly payroll and more from Pebl.
- [What Is Business Immigration?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/business-immigration): Business immigration is when workers move abroad for work by securing visas and permits. Learn its benefits, challenges, and more with Pebl.
- [What Is Business Process Outsourcing (BPO)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/business-process-outsourcing): Business process outsourcing, or BPO, is a strategy where organizations use subcontractors to improve efficiency, reduce costs, and optimize specialization. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is Career Mobility?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/career-mobility): Career mobility is when an employee moves into a new role, whether upward, laterally, or downward. Learn more about job mobility with Pebl.
- [What Is Centralized Payroll?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/centralized-payroll): Learn what centralized payroll is with Pebl. Find out how it helps employers manage global payroll efficiently from a single, compliant system.
- [What Is Co-Employment?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/co-employment): Co-employment is a contractual relationship whereby two parties share legal employer responsibilities of employees.
- [What Is Commission Pay?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/commission-pay): Commission pay is performance-based compensation tied to sales or results. Learn when it works and how to manage it with Pebl.
- [What Is Compa Ratio?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/compa-ratio): A compa ratio compares an employee’s salary to the midpoint of their pay range. Learn how to calculate it and use it for pay decisions with Pebl.
- [What Is Compensation Planning?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/compensation-planning): Compensation planning refers to when employers or HR teams plan and outline the terms and conditions of their employees’ salaries, benefits, and incentives.
- [What Is Compliance Management?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/compliance-management): Compliance management ensures company adherence to laws, regulations, standards, and internal policies governing its operations. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is Compliance Risk Management?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/compliance-risk-management): Compliance risk management means identifying and reducing losses that happen when businesses aren't compliant. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is Contract Labor?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/contract-labor): Contract labor refers to when a non-employee provides services to a company under the terms of a contract.
- [What Is Contract Staffing?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/contract-staffing): Contract staffing is an employment arrangement where a company hires an individual on a temporary or contract basis to fill a specific need.
- [What Is Contract to Hire?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/contract-to-hire): Contract to hire means having a worker take on a trial contract before offering full-time employment. Discover why employers use this strategy with Pebl.
- [What Is Core HR?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/core-hr): Learn what core HR is with Pebl. Find out why it’s essential for employers to build HR processes like payroll, compliance, and employee records.
- [What Is Coworking?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/what-is-coworking): Coworking is where people from different companies or teams share a physical space to work. Learn about coworking spaces from Pebl.
- [What Is Crypto Payroll?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/crypto-payroll): Crypto payroll is when companies pay employees using cryptocurrencies like Bitcoin instead of traditional fiat currencies. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is Cultural Intelligence (CQ)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/cultural-intelligence): Cultural intelligence (CQ) is the ability to understand, adapt to, and work across cultural contexts and communication styles. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is Deferred Compensation?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/deferred-compensation): Learn what deferred compensation is with Pebl. Find out how it works, and why employers use it to retain talent and manage payroll obligations.
- [What Is Deferred Revenue?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/deferred-revenue): Deferred revenue is recorded when businesses are paid before delivering their products or services. Explore how it works and why it’s key for reporting with Pebl.
- [What Is Direct Compensation?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/direct-compensation): Direct compensation refers to any monetary payments, rewards, and benefits an employee receives for their work.
- [What Is Earned Wage Access?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/earned-wage-access): Learn what earned wage access is with Pebl. Find out how to offer flexible pay solutions that improve retention and employee financial wellness.
- [What Is Employee Benefits Administration?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employee-benefits-administration): Employee benefits administration is the process of establishing and managing the benefits an organization offers its employees in a compensation package.
- [What Is Employee Data Protection?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employee-data-protection): Employee data protection keeps workforce information secure, compliant, and properly accessed. Protect employee data across hiring, payroll, and beyond.
- [What Is Employee Leasing?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employee-leasing): Employee leasing, or temporary leasing, is when a staffing firm supplies workers on a project-specific or temporary basis for a business.
- [What Is Employee Mobility?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employee-mobility): Employee mobility is the ability of an employee to move physically or professionally within an organization or career.
- [What Is Employee Time Tracking?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employee-time-tracking): Learn what employee time tracking is, why it’s important, and how to follow regulatory requirements in the US and abroad with Pebl.
- [What Is Employee Turnover?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employee-turnover): Define employee turnover and explore strategies and solutions for turnover mitigation. Pebl explains how to calculate employee turnover and more.
- [What Is Employee Upskilling?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employee-upskilling): Upskilling employees enables them to sharpen or broaden their skill sets. Learn the benefits and challenges of upskilling employees with Pebl.
- [What Is Employment Status?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employment-status): Employment status is the classification of the relationship between an employer and their employee. Learn employment status types and their differences.
- [What Is Employment Verification?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/employment-verification): An employment verification letter confirms an employee’s job status. Learn how to issue a compliant employment verification letter with Pebl.
- [What Is Endpoint Security?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/endpoint-security): Endpoint security is the practice of protecting devices from threats, unauthorized access, and data loss. Learn how it works and see what to prioritize.
- [What Is Equity Compensation?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/equity-compensation): Learn what equity compensation is, how it works, and the pros and cons of offering stock-based pay to attract and retain top talent with Pebl.
- [What Is ESG Compliance?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/esg-compliance): ESG compliance means meeting environmental, social, and governance standards. Learn its importance, regulations, and more with Pebl.
- [What Is Expatriate Compensation?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/expatriate-compensation): Expatriate compensation packages, also known as expat packages, compensate employees who move abroad for work. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is Fair Workweek?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/fair-workweek): Learn about fair workweek laws, which protect workers from unstable schedules and last-minute changes. Explore key rules and employer compliance requirements.
- [What Is FMLA?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/family-medical-leave-act): Learn about the Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA), eligibility requirements, rules, employer responsibilities, meaning, and more with Pebl.
- [What Is Foreign Earned Income Exclusion?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/foreign-earned-income-exclusion): Foreign earned income exclusion removes income earned and already taxed in a foreign country from U.S. taxable income. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is Form 1099-MISC?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/form-1099-misc): Form 1099-MISC is a tax document for reporting various types of miscellaneous, non-wage compensation to the IRS and the recipient of those payments.
- [What Is Form 1099-NEC?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/form-1099-nec): Form 1099-NEC is a tax document businesses use to report payments made to non-employees, such as contractors, freelancers, consultants, and vendors.
- [What Is Form 941?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/form-941): Learn what Form 941 is with Pebl. Explore filing deadlines, tips, and how U.S. employers use it to report federal payroll taxes each quarter.
- [What Is Form SS-8?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/form-ss-8): Form SS-8 is a document that requests a decision on a U.S. worker's status for federal employment taxes and income tax withholding purposes.
- [What Is FTE (Full-Time Equivalent)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/full-time-equivalent-fte): FTE (full-time equivalent) calculates total hours employees work. Explore the meaning of FTEs and full-time employees with Pebl.
- [What Is Furlough Leave?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/furlough-leave): Learn what furlough leave is, when employers use it, and how to manage the legal, financial, and HR challenges that come with it with Pebl.
- [What is FUTA?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/futa-tax): FUTA is an acronym for the United States Federal Unemployment Tax Act, which requires employers to pay unemployment tax. Learn how to calculate FUTA.
- [What Is GDPR Compliance?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/gdpr-compliance): Learn what GDPR (General Data Protection Regulation) compliance is and why it’s vital to keep your business compliant with Pebl.
- [What is Geographic Arbitrage?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/geographic-arbitrage): Geographic arbitrage is when you live in a low-cost area while earning the same income as you would in a high-cost region. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is Geographical Discrimination?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/geographical-discrimination): Geographical discrimination refers to the unfair treatment or prejudice against individuals based on their geographic location or country of origin.
- [What Is Global Compensation?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/global-compensation): Global compensation is all forms of compensation paid to employees working abroad. Learn what makes a good global compensation strategy with Pebl.
- [What Is Global Employment Outsourcing?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/global-employment-outsourcing): Global employment outsourcing enables companies to hire, pay, and manage an international workforce without establishing foreign entities.
- [What Is Global Fluency?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/global-fluency): Global fluency is the ability to effectively and seamlessly operate in a global or international context.
- [What Is Global Human Resource Management?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/global-human-resource-management): Global human resource management (GHRM) is the coordination of human resources (HR) functions in an international context. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What is Global Mobility?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/global-mobility): Global mobility is a business policy that enables employees to work from anywhere. Learn how to offer global mobility for your team with Pebl.
- [What Is Global Payroll?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/global-payroll): Global payroll is managing employee compensation in multiple countries, while complying with local laws and currencies. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is Global PEO?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/global-peo): A global PEO enables companies to hire and pay talent anywhere in the world quickly, compliantly, and without the burden of establishing a foreign legal entity.
- [What Is Global Recruitment?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/global-recruitment): Global recruitment is the process of finding and hiring people from around the world. Learn more about international recruiting with Pebl.
- [What Is Global Workforce Management?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/global-workforce-management): Global workforce management allows organizations to oversee and optimize their workforce globally. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is Gross Income?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/gross-income): [node:suGet the definition of gross income with Pebl. Understand gross vs. net income, how to calculate gross income, and how to find gross income.
- [What Is Gross to Net?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/gross-to-net): Gross-to-net (GTN) is a payroll process that determines an employee’s take-home pay after removing taxes and deductions from gross income.
- [What Is Headcount?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/headcount): Learn what headcount is and how it differs from FTE. Find out why workforce tracking matters for planning, budgeting, and organizational decision-making from Pebl.
- [What Is Holiday Pay?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/holiday-pay): Holiday pay is compensation for public holidays. Explore U.S. practices, global requirements, and key considerations for legal compliance with Pebl.
- [What Is HR Analytics?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hr-analytics): HR analytics uses workforce data to evaluate performance, predict trends, and optimize human resource decisions. Implement HR analytics with Pebl.
- [What Is HR Automation?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hr-automation): HR automation leverages digital tools and software to streamline repetitive HR tasks. Learn how to utilize HR automation and minimize human intervention with Pebl.
- [What is HR Change Management?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hr-change-management): HR change management is the process of guiding employees through organizational change. Learn to use it to support teams with Pebl.
- [What Is HR Compliance?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/what-is-hr-compliance): Explore what HR compliance is, why it matters, and how to avoid legal risks with Pebl. Get practical tips for maintaining compliance globally.
- [What Is HR Reporting?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hr-reporting): Learn what HR reporting is with Pebl. Discover why it matters, and how HR teams use data to track headcount, performance, and compliance.
- [What Is HR Software?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hr-software): Human resources (HR) software is a tool that helps manage employees and HR-related processes. Learn about HR solutions and technology with Pebl.
- [What Is HR Tech?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hr-tech): HR technology is the digital tools, software, and automation systems used to streamline human resource processes. Implement HR tech with Pebl.
- [What Is HR Transformation?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hr-transformation): HR transformation overhauls human resource operations making them more agile and data-driven. Align your HR with business outcomes with Pebl.
- [What Is Human Capital Management (HCM)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/human-capital-management): Human capital management (HCM) are the tools and practices used to organize, manage, recruit, train, and retain employees. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is Imputed Income?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/imputed-income): Learn what imputed income is with Pebl. Discover how it’s calculated, and why the value of non-cash benefits must be reported by employers.
- [What Is Indirect Compensation?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/indirect-compensation): Indirect compensation refers to all non-monetary benefits employees receive in addition to their base and supplemental pay.
- [What Is International Double Taxation?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/international-double-taxation): International double taxation is when you are taxed twice on the same income. Learn how this happens to Americans working abroad with Pebl’s glossary.
- [What Is International Employment Law?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/international-employment-law): International employment law governs employee and employer rights. Global employment law includes contracts, hours, and more. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What is International Employment?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/international-employment): International employment is working abroad, for an international company in the U.S., or having a job that requires travel. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is International Labor Law?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/international-labor-law): Taking your business operations overseas requires a basic understanding of international labor law. Learn what it is and more with Pebl.
- [What Is International Payroll Outsourcing?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/international-payroll-outsourcing): International payroll outsourcing is hiring a service to manage payroll for a company’s employees in different countries. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is IoT Device Management?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/iot-device-management): Learn about IoT device management: how to onboard, monitor, update, secure, and retire connected devices at scale, and why it matters.
- [What Is IR35 Legislation?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/ir35-legislation): IR35 legislation ensures that UK contractors who would otherwise be considered employees pay appropriate tax rates. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is IRS Form 1096?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/form-1096): Form 1096 is a summary form that U.S. businesses use to report any tax forms that report non-employee compensation to the IRS by mail.
- [What Is IRS Form 673?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/form-673): Form 673 is an Internal Revenue Service (IRS) tax form to claim an exemption from U.S. income tax withholding a U.S. employee earns on foreign wages abroad.
- [What Is IRS Form W-9?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/form-w-9): W-9 for contractors is a U.S. IRS tax form that collects and verifies taxpayer info from non-employees receiving income. Learn more from Pebl.
- [What Is ISO 27001?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/iso-27001): Learn what ISO 27001 is, how certification works, and why it matters for security, compliance, payroll, HR, and global teams.
- [What Is Job Classification?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/job-classification): Job classification is the process of grouping roles by responsibilities and skill level. Learn how it supports fair pay, compliance, and workforce planning.
- [What Is Joint Employment?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/joint-employment): Joint employment is when two organizations share control over one employee’s work. Learn what it means, how to spot risks, and how to protect your team.
- [What Is Labor Law?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/labor-law): Labor law refers to regulations between employers, employees and labor unions. Explore labor law meaning, who they protect and more with Pebl.
- [What Is Legal Entity Rationalization?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/legal-entity-rationalization): Legal entity rationalization (LER) simplifies a company's legal structure to improve efficiency and reduce costs. Learn the benefits with Pebl.
- [What Is Managed Payroll?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/managed-payroll): Managed payroll allows businesses to outsource their payroll and tax compliance to a third-party provider. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is Market Expansion?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/market-expansion): Market expansion is a company's growth strategy to increase its market share, operations, customer base, and presence in existing locations or new markets.
- [What Is Maternity Leave?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/maternity-leave): Maternity leave is the period of time in which a new mother takes off work before and after the birth of their child.
- [What Is Medicare Tax?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/medicare-tax): Learn what Medicare tax covers. Find out how to handle additional taxes for high earners, and how U.S. employers can stay compliant with Pebl.
- [What Is Misclassification?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/misclassification): Misclassification refers to the act of assigning an individual or something to the wrong group or category.
- [What Is Mobile Device Management (MDM)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/mobile-device-management-mdm): Mobile device management is software that secures and manages work devices from one place. Learn how MDM can help simplify control.
- [What Is Multi-Country Payroll?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/multi-country-payroll): Multi-country payroll refers to managing and processing payroll for employees in different countries with different tax and employment regulations. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is Net Pay?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/net-pay): Net pay is the money earned after removing all deductions from gross pay. Explore the definition and difference between net vs. gross pay with Pebl.
- [What Is Off-Cycle Payroll?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/off-cycle-payroll): Off-cycle payroll refers to when an employer pays employees on an ad hoc basis instead of on a regular payroll schedule. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is Offboarding?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/offboarding): Offboarding is the process of managing and facilitating an employee’s departure. Discover offboarding best practices, benefits, and more with Pebl.
- [What Is Offshoring?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/offshoring): Offshoring is the relocation of business operations, functions, or services to a new country. Get the offshoring definition and more with Pebl.
- [What Is Onboarding?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/onboarding): Onboarding is the process of integrating new employees into a company and familiarizing them with their position, job requirements, company policies, and culture.
- [What Is Overtime?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/what-is-overtime): Overtime is work that exceeds an employee's regularly scheduled work hours. Learn how overtime works and how overtime pay is calculated with Pebl.
- [What Is Paid Time Off (PTO)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/pto-paid-time-off): Get the essentials of paid time off (PTO), including the definition of PTO, how to calculate it, accrual, common PTO types, and more with Pebl.
- [What Is Parental Leave?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/parental-leave): Parental leave provides time off from work following the birth or adoption of a child. Learn about paid parental leave by country with Pebl.
- [What Is Pass-Through Taxation?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/pass-through-taxation): Learn what pass-through taxation is with Pebl. Find out how it works, and why small business owners and remote employers can benefit from it.
- [What Is Paternity Leave?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/paternity-leave): Paternity leave is a type of employee leave that allows fathers or partners to take time off from work to care for their new child.
- [What Is Pay Equity?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/pay-equity): Learn the importance of pay equity for global teams with Pebl. Explore legal obligations, best practices, and how to close unjustified wage gaps.
- [What Is Pay Parity?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/pay-parity): Pay parity means equal pay for equal work. Learn what it is, why it matters for compliance and equity, and how to achieve pay parity globally with Pebl.
- [What Is Payment in Lieu of Notice (PILON)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/payment-in-lieu-of-notice): Payment in lieu of notice (PILON) is the compensation a terminated employee receives in the placement of working through their notice period.
- [What Is Payroll Automation?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/payroll-automation): Learn what payroll automation is with Pebll. Discover how to streamline payroll, reduce errors, and stay compliant with automated payroll.
- [What Is Payroll Compliance?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/what-is-payroll-compliance): Payroll compliance is the process of following all federal, state, and local laws that govern how employees are paid. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is Payroll Processing?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/payroll-processing): Payroll processing is how employers calculate and distribute employee pay. Learn the steps, compliance risks, and why accuracy is critical with Pebl.
- [What Is Payroll Remittance?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/payroll-remittance): Learn what payroll remittance is with Pebl. Find out how employers handle payroll tax payments, deductions, and compliance reporting.
- [What Is Payroll Transformation?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/payroll-transformation): Payroll transformation means overhauling payroll systems to boost accuracy, efficiency, and compliance. Discover how it works with Pebl.
- [What Is People Analytics?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/people-analytics): People analytics is the use of employee data to guide talent and business decisions. Learn why it matters for employers and workers with Pebl.
- [What Is Per Diem?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/what-is-per-diem): Per diem is an employee allowance for lodging, meals, and incidental expenses incurred when traveling. Learn about per diem rates and more from Pebl.
- [What Is PERM Labor Certification?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/perm-labor-certification): A Permanent Labor Certification (PERM) allows employers to hire foreign workers for permanent employment in the U.S. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is Post-Tax Deduction?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/post-tax-deduction): Post-tax deduction, or after-tax deduction, refers to expenses or contributions subtracted from an employee's income after taxes have been withheld.
- [What Is Pre-Tax Income?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/pre-tax-income): Pre-tax income represents a company’s net income before subtracting income taxes but still includes deductions related to operating expenses and interest.
- [What Is Profit Sharing?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/profit-sharing): Profit sharing is a compensation strategy where employees receive a share of company profits. Learn how it works, common types, and benefits with Pebl.
- [What Is Quiet Hiring?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/quiet-hiring): Learn how quiet hiring fills roles and fulfill the needs of a business without hiring new talent. Learn about quiet hiring in the workplace with Pebl.
- [What Is Real-Time Payroll?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/real-time-payroll): Real-time payroll, or real-time processing, allows employers to report and process wages instantly. Learn about its pros and cons with Pebl.
- [What Is Reboarding?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/reboarding): Reboarding is when returning employees are reintroduced to the workplace. Learn how it helps retention and workforce reintegration with Pebl.
- [What Is Record of Employment (ROE)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/record-of-employment): Learn what a record of employment is, when employers must issue one in Canada, how it affects EI claims, and what businesses need to know to stay organized and accurate.
- [What Is Remote Work?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/remote-work): Remote work is a flexible arrangement that allows employees to work outside of a traditional office and instead work from home or coworking spaces.
- [What Is Retro Pay?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/retro-pay): Retro pay, or retroactive pay, is the compensation an employer owes an employee due to a payment shortfall during the previous pay period.
- [What Is Severance Pay?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/severance-pay): Severance pay is compensation provided when employment ends. Learn when it’s offered, the amount, and why accurate calculation matters with Pebl.
- [What Is Shadow Payroll?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/shadow-payroll): Shadow payroll allows employers to stay compliant with local taxes while paying employees from a different country. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is Short-Term Disability?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/short-term-disability): Learn what short-term disability is, how it works, and how it differs from long-term disability, including what it covers and when employees can use it.
- [What Is SHRM Certification?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/shrm-certification): Learn what SHRM certification is with Pebl. Find out how it works, and why employers should see the benefits of certified HR professionals.
- [What Is Single Touch Payroll in Australia?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/single-touch-payroll): Single Touch Payroll (STP) is Australia’s mandatory real-time payroll reporting system. Learn how to keep your payroll compliant with Pebl.
- [What Is Skills-Based Hiring?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/skills-based-hiring): Skills-based hiring prioritizes a candidate’s skills and competencies over traditional credentials. Learn about skills-based hiring with Pebl.
- [What Is Sourcing in HR?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/hr-sourcing): In HR, sourcing means proactively searching for qualified job candidates rather than waiting for talent to apply on their own. Learn HR sourcing best practices.
- [What Is Statutory Sick Pay?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/statutory-sick-pay): Learn how statutory sick pay works, who qualifies, how it’s calculated, employer obligations, and why local rules matter across countries.
- [What Is Strategic HR Management?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/strategic-hr-management): Strategic HR management means aligning HR with long-term business objectives. Learn its importance, benefits, and key initiatives with Pebl.
- [What Is Supplemental Pay?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/supplemental-pay): Supplemental pay is an employee's additional compensation on top of their regular base earnings. Learn examples and the importance of supplemental pay.
- [What Is Talent Arbitrage?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/talent-arbitrage): Talent arbitrage is the hiring of skilled workers where labor costs are lower, to reduce workforce costs. Learn how talent arbitrage works with Pebl.
- [What Is Talent Density?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/talent-density): Talent density is the proportion of high-performing employees within a company’s workforce. Learn why it matters and how to measure with Pebl.
- [What Is Tax Equalization?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/tax-equalization): Tax equalization adjusts tax owed when living and working abroad to avoid double taxation. Learn about tax equalization for expats with Pebl.
- [What Is Telework?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/telework): Telework is an arrangement allowing employees to work outside the office. Learn how it differs from remote work and supports productivity with Pebl.
- [What Is the B1/B2 Visa?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/b1-b2-visa): The B-1/B-2 visa allows foreign nationals to travel to the U.S. for business and tourism in the same trip. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is the Corporate Sustainability Reporting Directive (CSRD)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/csrd): The Corporate Sustainability Reporting Directive (CSRD) requires EU companies to disclose information about their environmental and social impacts. Learn more.
- [What is the EU Platform Work Directive (PWD)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/platform-work-directive): Learn what the EU Platform Work Directive (PWD) means for gig workers and global employers. Understand key compliance steps with Pebl.
- [What Is the Fair Work Act and the Fair Work Commission (FWC)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/fair-work-act-and-the-fair-work-commission-fwc): Learn what the Fair Work Act and Fair Work Commission (FWC) are, how they shape workplace rights, and what employers need to know to stay compliant in Australia.
- [What Is the Global Marketplace?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/global-marketplace): The global marketplace refers to all buyers and sellers unencumbered by borders. Learn more about the global marketplace with Pebl.
- [What Is the Labor Market?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/labor-market): The labor market is the availability of employment and labor in terms of supply and demand. Understand its role in the overall economy with Pebl.
- [What Is the Marginal Revenue Formula?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/marginal-revenue-formula): Learn about the marginal revenue formula and how it shows the extra revenue from each additional unit. Calculate it and use it to drive smarter growth decisions.
- [What Is the Minimum Wages Act?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/minimum-wages-act): Minimum Wages Act requires employers in India to meet notified minimum pay rates. Explore key rules, risks, and payroll steps now.
- [What Is the VP of People?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/vp-of-people): A VP of People is an executive who oversees HR tasks like talent acquisition, employee relations, and company culture. Learn more with Pebl.
- [What Is Time to Fill?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/time-to-fill): Time to fill measures how long a job stays open from requisition to hiring. Learn why it’s a key hiring metric for workforce planning with Pebl.
- [What Is Time to Hire?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/time-to-hire): Time to hire measures the time between a candidate’s application and hiring. Learn why it matters and how it differs from time to fill with Pebl.
- [What Is Time to Market (TTM)?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/time-to-market): Time to market (TTM) is the time it takes from the conception of a product to its release on the market. Learn about TTM strategy with Pebl.
- [What Is Total Remuneration?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/total-remuneration): Total remuneration is the complete sum of an employee's annual compensation package. Learn how to calculate total remuneration and more with Pebl.
- [What Is Unlimited PTO?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/unlimited-pto): Explore the ins and outs of unlimited PTO with Pebl. Discover how it works, and if it’s the right policy for your company’s culture.
- [What Is Unpaid Time Off?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/unpaid-time-off): Unpaid time off (UTO), also called unpaid leave, refers to an employee’s time away from work without pay. Learn the benefits and downsides of providing UTO.
- [What Is Upskilling and Reskilling?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/upskilling-reskilling): Upskilling and reskilling apply to talent development, in which employees learn new skills that help them expand their knowledge in their career path.
- [What Is Vesting?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/vesting): Vesting is the process of earning ownership of benefits like equity or retirement contributions. Learn how vesting works and why it matters with Pebl.
- [What Is Virtual Bookkeeping?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/virtual-bookkeeping): Virtual bookkeeping is remote financial recordkeeping using cloud tools. Learn how it works and why businesses prefer it over traditional bookkeeping.
- [What Is Visa Sponsorship?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/visa-sponsorship): Visa sponsorship refers to the process where an individual or organization legally supports a foreign national to enter or stay in another country.
- [What Is Voluntary Time Off?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/vto-voluntary-time-off): Voluntary Time Off (VTO) is an unpaid, optional leave offered during slow periods. Learn how VTO works, when it’s used, and how it differs from PTO.
- [What Is Wage Compression?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/wage-compression): Learn what wage compression is with Pebl. Explore how it affects compensation fairness and strategies employers use to address it across teams.
- [What Is Work Authorization?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/work-authorization): Work authorization, or employment authorization, allows foreign nationals to legally work in another country. Explore forms needed and more with Pebl.
- [What Is Workforce Agility?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/workforce-agility): Workforce agility is a company’s ability to adapt quickly to business changes. Workforce agility prioritizes employee flexibility, responsiveness, and adaptability.
- [What Is Workforce Mobility?](https://hellopebl.com/glossary/workforce-mobility): Workforce mobility is the ability of a company’s workforce to move and work from one location to another.

## Integrations

- [ADP Workforce Now](https://hellopebl.com/integrations/adp-workforce-now): Pebl’s ADP Workforce Now integration helps mid-to-large global teams unify payroll, compliance, employee data, onboarding, and workforce management.
